<h2>Web Chat: The Cool Feature</h2>

<p>
    Web chat is particularly powerful because of how it integrates with your website and client records:
</p>

<h3>Real-Time Communication</h3>

<p>
    When someone visits your website and starts a chat, you see their messages instantly in Quickfire. No refreshing, no checking—messages appear as they type.
</p>

<h3>Context Linking</h3>

<p>
    When a web chat conversation ends, Quickfire automatically:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Links the transcript to the client record (if they're a client)</li>
    <li>Creates a client record if they're new (if configured)</li>
    <li>Preserves the full conversation history</li>
    <li>Makes it easy to see all communications with that person</li>
</ul>

<p>
    This means when you open a client record later, you can see the web chat conversation right there alongside emails, calls, and other interactions.
</p>

<h3>Seamless Workflow</h3>

<p>
    You can be working on a renewal or client record, see a web chat come in, reply to it, and continue your work—all without switching applications or losing context.
</p>

