<h2>Staying Organized</h2>

<p>
    The chat panel helps you stay organized:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Conversation list</strong> – All your conversations are listed so you can find them easily</li>
    <li><strong>Search</strong> – Search through message history to find specific conversations</li>
    <li><strong>Context preservation</strong> – Conversations are linked to clients, renewals, or other records when relevant</li>
    <li><strong>Full history</strong> – Nothing gets lost—all messages are saved</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Even after a busy day, you can reopen any conversation and see the full history.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the conversation list showing multiple conversations organized by channel. Show search functionality if available. Include examples of conversations linked to client records. -->

<h2>Tips for Using Chat</h2>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Check unread counts regularly</strong> – Glance at the badges to see where attention is needed</li>
    <li><strong>Reply promptly to web chats</strong> – Website visitors expect quick responses</li>
    <li><strong>Use staff chat for quick questions</strong> – Faster than email for internal communication</li>
    <li><strong>Keep context</strong> – The chat panel stays open while you work, so you can reply without losing your place</li>
    <li><strong>Review web chat transcripts</strong> – Check linked conversations when working with clients</li>
    <li><strong>Attach files when helpful</strong> – Share documents directly through chat</li>
</ul>

