<h2>Keyboard Shortcuts</h2>

<p>
    The chat panel supports keyboard shortcuts for faster communication:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Enter</strong> – Send message</li>
    <li><strong>Tab</strong> – Switch between input fields or conversations (depending on context)</li>
    <li><strong>Arrow keys</strong> – Navigate conversation list</li>
</ul>

<p>
    These shortcuts help you communicate quickly without taking your hands off the keyboard.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: A simple reference card or diagram showing the keyboard shortcuts. Use keyboard icons or visual representations of the keys. -->

<h2>Works Alongside Your Tasks</h2>

<p>
    The chat panel is designed to work alongside your other Quickfire tasks:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Stays in context</strong> – You can have a client record open and chat at the same time</li>
    <li><strong>Non-intrusive</strong> – Chat appears in a panel, not a popup, so it doesn't block your work</li>
    <li><strong>Linked conversations</strong> – Web chats and SMS automatically link to client records</li>
    <li><strong>Full history access</strong> – See all communications when viewing a client</li>
</ul>

<p>
    This design keeps everything in one place so you don't have to switch between applications or lose track of what you were doing.
    </p>

